        "rcsb_pubmed_central_id": "PMC6269658",
        "rcsb_pubmed_doi": "10.3390/molecules181114414",
        "rcsb_pubmed_abstract_text": "The first cyclic analog of a metallothionein (MT) was prepared and analyzed by UV and (magnetic) circular dichroism spectroscopy, ESI-MS as well as NMR spectroscopy. Results reveal that the evaluated cyclic γ-E(c)-1 domain of the wheat MT E(c)-1 retains its ability to coordinate two Zn(II) or Cd(II) ions and adopts a three-dimensional structure that is highly similar to the one of the linear wild-type form. However, the reduced flexibility of the protein backbone facilitates structure solution significantly and results in a certain stabilization of metal binding to the protein.",
        "rcsb_pubmed_affiliation_info": [
          "Institute of Inorganic Chemistry, University of Zurich, Winterthurerstrasse 190, Zurich CH-8057, Switzerland. freisinger@aci.uzh.ch."
        ]
      },
